            "v": "S&P 500 performance chart",
            "zh": "标普 500 指数实时走势图"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " onto the blackboard. It was a sea of mostly red boxes. One of the 14-year-old students quickly answered, “Trash.” She was not wrong. It was a rubbish morning for the index. Varga "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "adjusted",
            "ref": "v-adjust"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the chart to show the S&P’s rise over the past month and then the past six months. The students nodded at the green boxes as Varga explained the advantages of long-term "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "investing",
            "zh": "投资"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Personal-"
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "finance",
            "ref": "v-finance"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " courses are spreading across the US. Half of its 50 states have made taking a financial-literacy course a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "requirement",
            "ref": "v-requirement"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for high school graduation. To be sure, students in these classes learn more than how to buy and sell shares. They also learn how to budget, bank properly, and manage their credit. The courses cover comparison shopping and the basics of planning and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "tracking",
            "ref": "v-track"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " daily expenses."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Young people badly need these courses. Studies have shown that most teens score low in financial literacy. Students who take personal-finance courses, however, are less likely to borrow money. When they do borrow money, they choose less expensive products. These students are also less likely to have credit card debt, and they have higher credit scores."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“It would have been nice to have had this class when I was 20,” said Varga. She experienced some financial trouble as a young adult. She then learnt the subjects she now teaches and improved her own money management skills. “I want them to do better than my generation did.”"
          }
        ]
      }
